Hey @tarekgh,
So if I got it right, the proposal is:

```csharp
private static int FindBraceIndex(string message, char searchedBrace, int startIndex, int endIndex)
{
    Debug.Assert(searchedBrace is '{' or '}');

    int braceIndex = -1;
    int scanIndex = startIndex;

    while (scanIndex < endIndex)
    {
        char current = message[scanIndex];

        if (current is '{' or '}')
        {
            if (searchedBrace == '}')
            {
                return current == '}' ? scanIndex : -2;
            }

            char currentBrace = current;
            int scanIndexBeforeSkip = scanIndex;
            while (current == currentBrace && ++scanIndex < endIndex)
            {
                current = message[scanIndex];
            }

            int bracesCount = scanIndex - scanIndexBeforeSkip;
            if (bracesCount % 2 != 0)
            {
                return currentBrace == '{' ? scanIndex - 1 : -2;
            }
        }
        else
        {
            scanIndex++;
        }
    }

    return braceIndex;
}
```

If so, I added it to the solution, it passed all current tests :)

On the other hand, I think I found a weird behavior on this new method version, that is actually "fixed" by how (the order) `ExtractTemplates` calls it.

Take for example the string template: `"}}prefix"`.

Because `ExtractTemplates` first calls `FindBraceIndex` looking for an `{`, it skips the first `}}` and because it never finds `{`, it returns `-1`, causing the method to accept it as a valid template with no arguments - which is the correct behavior here.

But if we *first* had called `FindBraceIndex` looking for an `}`, this method would return the index `0` - which is incorrect, since it should return `-1`, because it should skip the `}}`.

> the method I previously committed returns `-1`, in this case.

In fact, this version is indeed optimized and cleaner, but it somehow depends on the previous call issued by `ExtractTemplates` to be correct. So, my question is: is this temporal coupling between the method calls ok? Or the method `FindBraceIndex` should behave well "isolated"?

I'd appreciate your input here 👍 Thanks!
